.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt M4 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm m4
.Nd macro processor (bounded POSIX core)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl D Ar name Ns Op = Ns Ar value
.Op Fl U Ar name
.Op Fl I Ar dir
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility reads the file operands in order, or standard input when no operand is given or the
operand is
.Sq - ,
expands macro calls, and writes the result to standard output.
Definitions and diversions persist across file operands.
.Pp
The default beginning and ending quote strings are
.Sq \`
and
.Sq ' ;
quoted text is copied without macro expansion, and nested quote pairs are matched while finding
the closing quote.
Comments begin with
.Sq #
and end at a newline; they are copied without expansion.
.Pp
The following options are supported:
.Bl -tag -width changequote
.It Fl D Ar name Ns Op = Ns Ar value
Define
.Ar name
as
.Ar value ,
or as the empty string when the assignment is omitted.
.It Fl U Ar name
Remove every definition of
.Ar name .
.It Fl I Ar dir
Search
.Ar dir
for files named by
.Ic include
before the process path.
.El
.Pp
A macro call is a name token immediately followed by an optional parenthesized argument list.
Arguments are expanded while they are collected; unquoted commas separate arguments and nested
parentheses are retained.
The substitutions
.Va $0
through
.Va $9 ,
.Va $# ,
.Va $*
and
.Va $@
are supported.
.Pp
The following built-in macros are implemented:
.Bl -tag -width changequote
.It Ic define
Define or replace a macro.
.It Ic undefine
Remove all definitions of the named macros.
.It Ic defn
Expand to the quoted definition of the named macros.
.It Ic pushdef , popdef
Push and pop definitions.
.It Ic dnl
Discard input through the next newline.
.It Ic include
Process the named file; the
.Fl I
directories are searched first.
.It Ic changequote , changecom
Change the quote or comment delimiters.
.It Ic ifdef , ifelse
Select expansion text.
.It Ic incr , decr
Increment or decrement a decimal integer.
.It Ic eval
Evaluate a signed-integer expression with C-like operators and parentheses.
.It Ic substr , index , translit
Substring, position and character-translation operations.
.It Ic divert , undivert
Write to, or emit from, numbered diversion buffers.
.El
.Pp
The
.Ic syscmd
and
.Ic esyscmd
macros are not implemented; calling either is a usage error.
The omitted built-ins are
.Ic divnum ,
.Ic dumpdef ,
.Ic errprint ,
.Ic len ,
.Ic m4exit ,
.Ic m4wrap ,
.Ic mkstemp ,
.Ic shift ,
.Ic sinclude ,
.Ic sysval ,
.Ic traceon
and
.Ic traceoff .
The
.Fl s
option and the optional result-radix and minimum-digit arguments of
.Ic eval
are not implemented.
.Pp
On the target image, standard input is read from the console terminal; there is no general
process pipeline handle yet.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
An invalid or unsupported program exits with status 2; a file, include or expansion failure exits
with status 1.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr awk 1 ,
.Xr grep 1 ,
.Xr sed 1
.Sh STANDARDS
The bounded core follows the POSIX.1-2024
.Xr m4 1
expansion model, with the
.Fl I
extension.
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility first appeared in Version 7 AT&T UNIX.
